{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-31",
  "mode": "hybrid",
  "description": "Three vehicles with source-directed velocity arrows and the printed 200 km/h reference segment. Vehicle identities belong to artwork; directions and the scale belong to deterministic geometry.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/6p/figures/fig-31.png",
      "sha256": "9e047ee0b94f9fe1c9cd36aab5216e6c10309a9711dc6e445872327d95a12dcd"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "phy6-c3-s3",
        "text": "物体的速度不仅用数值，并且还需用方向来表征。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy6-c3-s3",
        "text": "例如，要想知道从出发城市起飞的飞机在飞行了两个小时之后将位于何处，就不仅需要知道它的速度是多大，还要知道它飞行的方向如何。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy6-c3-s3",
        "text": "为了进行比较，我们举出几个没有方向的物理量的例子：时间、物体的体积、1立方厘米空气中的分子数等。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy6-c3-s3",
        "text": "在图上，物体的速度用一个箭头来表示（图31）。"
      }
    ],
    "inventory": [
      {
        "id": "source-aircraft",
        "description": "Opened the complete original PNG: one aircraft at lower left faces upper right, with a much longer oblique segmented arrow toward upper right. Modern artwork is unbranded and colored; the deterministic arrow preserves its orientation, segmented appearance and relative prominence. Canvas coordinates regularize the scanned drawing and are not newly supplied speed measurements. There are no printed point markers; hidden endpoints are construction anchors, not source points.",
        "objects": [
          "vehicles",
          "aircraft-arrow"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "aircraft-direction",
          "aircraft-connection"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source-car",
        "description": "The original upper-right passenger car faces left, beside a short left-pointing horizontal arrow. The modern car and the separate leftward arrow preserve that pairing.",
        "objects": [
          "vehicles",
          "car-arrow"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "car-direction",
          "car-connection"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source-truck",
        "description": "The original lower-right cargo truck has three visible wheel/axle positions, faces right, and has a short right-pointing horizontal arrow. The artwork preserves a three-axle truck and the deterministic arrow preserves the opposite direction to the car.",
        "objects": [
          "vehicles",
          "truck-arrow"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "truck-direction",
          "truck-connection"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source-scale",
        "description": "The source lower-left reference segment is horizontal and labelled 200 km/h. It remains a separate non-arrow segment with the same value and unit, translated to English notation. No derived individual vehicle speeds are added.",
        "objects": [
          "scale-line",
          "scale-label"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "scale-horizontal",
          "scale-length"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "modern-artwork",
        "description": "One generated image holds exactly the three source vehicles without annotation, road marks or additional semantic objects. Contemporary colors, wider vertical separation and an opaque white background are modern presentation choices, not source facts. The image is fitted without aspect-ratio distortion.",
        "objects": [
          "vehicles"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "one-artwork-layer"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
